  "note": "Opening the inventory on habbo.fr and walking its four tabs: furni, pets, badges, bots. The build is WIN63-202609091217-117204808, NOT the workspace target WIN63-202607011411-782849652, so the header ids below belong to that newer build and must not be read as ours -- each message carries its name, which is what resolves it. Four things this settles. (1) Every fragmented list here is numbered from zero: FurniList, PetInventory and Badges all arrive as totalFragments 1 / fragmentNo 0. (2) FurniList sends each item's id twice with opposite signs -- itemId negative and roomItemId positive for a floor item ('S') -- which is the mirror of what Vortex serializes; the client only enforces the relation (FurniModel.as:1482 tests -objectId == ref on the floor and objectId == ref on the wall), so both satisfy it, but which of the two a client flow sends to the server differs: .id goes to placement and AddItemsToTrade, .ref goes to MakeOffer, the recycler and wired trading. (3) A non-rented item carries secondsToExpiration -1 and flatId -1, not zero -- the client sets isRented from secondsToExpiration > -1 and then suppresses grouping for a rented item, so a zero there would mark the whole inventory rented. (4) The badge tab gets HabboUserBadges unprompted alongside Badges; the client asks for nothing between GetBadges and the two replies. Every badge in both messages reports ownerCount 1000 and badgeRarityId 0, confirming the four-field badge layout. The account has 2 floor items, no pets and no bots, so the pet and bot bodies are only established as empty here.",
